Well, consider note taking to remember where certain levels are (for
example the entrance to the Mines or Vlad's Tower). I normally jot these
down on a piece of paper, as well as the intrinsics I already have.

The game does not record them for you, so it's imperative to write them
down. Your character would remember he had them, but since the game
doesn't show you, you must remember them as well.

If the wizard mode feature of showing known locations would be extended
to normal mode, adding special rooms et cetera once you've discovered
them, I would stop taking these notes, and I would not resume taking
these notes if a mind flayer wiped those memories from my character's
mind, since then, the game obviously means to not let you remember them.
In that case, I would just do what I always do in such a case: backtrack
through all levels I already visited, including side branches, and
remapping everything.

( By the way, if I still recalled them myself, I wouldn't purposely act
as if I did not. )

